      "observed": "The PWM2 channel to servo header J8 pin 3 is drawn with a 100 µF capacitor C6 in the signal path next to J8 pin 3 and R14, while the corresponding 1 kΩ series resistor R4 is not present.",
      "expected": "The specification requires R4 to be a 1 kΩ series resistor from PWM2 to J8 pin 3, mirroring R3 from PWM1 to J3 pin 3. The 100 µF capacitors are specified only as C1–C4 on the servo power rail.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "C6 100u (on the PWM2 line adjacent to J8 pin 3 and R14 0)"
        },
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "R3 1k (on the PWM1 line to J3 pin 3)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "R3, R4 | 1k each | Series resistors from the PWM1/PWM2 GPIO nets to J3 pin 3 / J8 pin 3 respectively."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The PWM2/tilt servo signal is blocked or heavily loaded by a 100 µF capacitor instead of being buffered through 1 kΩ; PWM2 servo control will fail, and in serial mode the shared TTL bus is also loaded by the capacitor.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic contains a component substitution error: C6, a 100 µF capacitor, is placed on the PWM2/J8-pin3 signal path where the specified R4 1 kΩ series resistor is missing."
}

